# Structure

Always follow DRY.

Always follow SOLID.

Separation of concerns is a priority.

Do not place different types of structures in a single file. Constants, helper functions, objects, schemas, services, and similar pieces each live in a file dedicated to that kind of structure.

Apply a layered approach. Always use folders to represent services, endpoints, and the other layers.

Static information must always be stored in the database and retrieved from there.
